<title>USA: US Treasury 2-year notes seen yielding 5.87 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 2-year notes seen yielding 5.87 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $17.5 billion in 2-year notes on Tuesday is expected to produce a yield near 5.87 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>The offering will settle February 28.</p>
<p>At 1256 EST/1756 GMT, yields on the two-year notes were quoted at 5.8725 percent in when-issued trade.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the notes is 1300 EST/1800 GMT and results are expected around 1345 EST/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>(( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679 ))</p>
</text>
